menu "Scroll Ack BLE board"

    choice SCRL_CAN_PINS
        prompt "Grove pins for TWAI TX and RX"
        default SCRL_CAN_PINS_UNCHECKED
        help
            The NanoH2 Grove port carries GPIO1 and GPIO2 to the Unit Mini CAN.
            The M5Stack sources disagree on which one is CAN TX. A wrong choice
            puts two outputs against each other.

            Before the first power-up with the Grove cable, measure continuity
            (nothing powered) from the NanoH2 Grove pins to TJA1051T/3 pin 1
            (TXD) and pin 4 (RXD) on the Mini CAN. TWAI TX goes to TXD.

            Until you choose, the firmware does not start the CAN controller
            and leaves both pins as inputs.

        config SCRL_CAN_PINS_UNCHECKED
            bool "Not checked yet (CAN stays off)"
        config SCRL_CAN_PINS_TX1_RX2
            bool "TX = GPIO1, RX = GPIO2"
        config SCRL_CAN_PINS_TX2_RX1
            bool "TX = GPIO2, RX = GPIO1"
    endchoice

    config SCRL_CAN_BITRATE
        int "CAN bit rate (bit/s)"
        default 500000
        help
            Tesla Vehicle CAN runs at 500 kbit/s.

endmenu
